  "description": "5 x Lime - Crown reduce the height and spread back to the previous reduction points 1.5m height and 1m spread. Remove Ivy from trunks and cut to ground level. Maintenance works in line with good arboricultural practice. Standing in Group G1 of Tree Preservation Order.\r\r1 x Large Yew - Crown reduce the spread towards property by 1.5m to give a 2.0m clearance. Maintenance works in line with good arboricultural practice. Standing in Area A1 of Tree Preservation Order.\r\r1 x Cedar - Remove dead wood. Maintenance works in line with good arboricultural practice. Standing in Area A1 of Tree Preservation Order.\r\r1 x Plum - Extensive decay in main fork just above ground level. Cut decayed stem close to ground level. Remove damaged branch growing towards property. Reduce the limbs leaning towards the property by 3.5m. Maintenance works in line with good arboricultural practice. Standing in Area A1 of Tree Preservation Order.",
